        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q_1",
          "label": "Question 1",
          "default": "How should I store the balm?"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "a_1",
          "label": "Answer 1",
          "default": "Keep the balm tightly closed and store it in a cool, dry place away from direct sunlight, excessive heat, and moisture. Always follow any storage instructions printed on the product label."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q_2",
          "label": "Question 2",
          "default": "How do I apply it?"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "a_2",
          "label": "Answer 2",
          "default": "Apply a small amount to clean, intact skin and massage gently until evenly distributed. Use only as directed on the product label."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q_3",
          "label": "Question 3",
          "default": "How often should I use it?"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "a_3",
          "label": "Answer 3",
          "default": "Follow the directions on the product label. Many customers include it in their morning and evening routines."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q_4",
          "label": "Question 4",
          "default": "Should I wash my hands?"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "a_4",
          "label": "Answer 4",
          "default": "Yes, unless you are applying the balm to your hands. Avoid touching your eyes, mouth, and other sensitive areas after application."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q_5",
          "label": "Question 5",
          "default": "Can I use it on wounds?"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "a_5",
          "label": "Answer 5",
          "default": "No. Apply the balm only to clean, intact skin. Do not apply it to open wounds, broken skin, or irritated areas."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q_6",
          "label": "Question 6",
          "default": "Is it suitable for sensitive skin?"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "a_6",
          "label": "Answer 6",
          "default": "Skin responses vary. Perform a small patch test first and discontinue use if redness, burning, or irritation occurs."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q_7",
          "label": "Question 7",
          "default": "Is it safe for everyone?"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "a_7",
          "label": "Answer 7",
          "default": "It is for external use only. Consult a healthcare professional before use on young children or if you have allergies or a medical condition."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q_8",
          "label": "Question 8",
          "default": "Can I use it while pregnant?"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "a_8",
          "label": "Answer 8",
          "default": "Consult your healthcare provider before using herbal topical products during pregnancy or while breastfeeding."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q_9",
          "label": "Question 9",
          "default": "What does it feel like?"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "a_9",
          "label": "Answer 9",
          "default": "The peppermint oil may create a refreshing cooling or warming sensation. Stop using it if the sensation becomes uncomfortable."
        },
        {
